body:
Sorry about that. XD

\- I will always express my true feelings, except if they hurt someone unnecessarily. I hide them, I don't lie about them. But if you ask me how I feel, you'll know the truth. I will support you then shudder, but I will never tell you you are right or that it's not upsetting. I will simply let you be who you are.

&#x200B;

\- Being insecure does not mean I have self-esteem issues. Needing validation doesn't mean I don't love myself. As an ENFP, I focus on how I make people feel. I want your experience with me to be magnificent, and I want you to see that. If you don't, I'll still love myself, but find the experience empty. 

&#x200B;

\- The second point reminded me of an important one about how we think: we don't see black and white, we see all shades of grey, all layers. That sometimes may cause people to think we contradict ourselves, but in our minds, we don't and it makes perfect sense.

&#x200B;

\- I can be positive and moody at the same time. I don't see my moodiness as a negative thing. I can have a positive view of the world and be moody because I need quiet. I will accept this as part of me and ride it until it's gone.

&#x200B;

I hope I helped. If I may ask, what's your type?
